//==========================================================================
//"The Knight"
//==========================================================================

BEGIN CHAPTER 6

"The Knight"
BOARD 1n4n1/48/1N4N1 WHITE
OK

"The Knight makes L-shaped moves.  Two squares along a rank or file, and then 
one square at a right angle."
BOARD 32/3N4/24 WHITE
OK

"For example, two squares along rank 4,"
BOARD 32/3N4/24 WHITE
OK

"and one square at a right angle along the b-file.  (It could also move to 
b5.)"
SLIDE d4 b4
OK

"Or, two squares along a file,"
SLIDE b4 b3
OK

"and then one square along rank 5.  (It could also move to a5.)"
SLIDE b3 b5
OK

SLIDE b5 c5
"Here are all the squares that a Knight on d4 can reach."
OK

BOARD 16/2N1N3/1N3N2/3N4/1N3N2/2N1N3/8 WHITE
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT c6
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT e6
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT c2
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT e2
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT f5
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT f3
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT b5
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT b3
"Notice that the Knight always lands on a square of a different color from 
the one on which it starts."
OK

"The Knight is special:  It jumps OVER pieces."
OK

BOARD 16/2r1N3/1N3N2/3N4/1P3N2/2N1N3/8 WHITE
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT e6
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT c2
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT e2
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT f5
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT f3
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT b5
"As always, you cannot move the Knight to a square containing another piece 
of the same color (such as b3)."
OK

"But you can capture an opponent's piece on the destination square."
OK

BOARD 16/2r5/8/3N4/1P6/8 WHITE
MOVE Nc6
"Knight takes Rook."
OK

BOARD 1N1N4/N3N3/2N5/N3N3/1N1N4/24 WHITE
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT d8
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT b8
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT b4
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT d4
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT a5
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT a7
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT e5
GHOST WHITE KNIGHT e7
"The Knight, like the Bishop, is considered less powerful than the Queen or 
Rook.  Even though it attacks fewer squares than a Bishop, its jumping 
ability makes it a valuable piece."
OK

END CHAPTER

