BEGIN CHAPTER 7

"The Pawn"
BOARD 8/pppppppp/32/PPPPPPPP/8 WHITE
OK

"All White Pawns start from rank 2."
BOARD 48/PPPPPPPP/8 WHITE
OK

"All Black Pawns start from rank 7."
BOARD 8/pppppppp/48 WHITE
OK

BOARD 8/pppppppp/32/PPPPPPPP/8 WHITE
"Pawns always move toward the opposite side of the board."
OK

"From its starting square, a Pawn may travel one or two squares forward."
OK

"Two squares..."
MOVE e4
OK

MOVE d6
"One Square..."
OK

MOVE f3
"One Square..."
OK

MOVE e5
"Two squares..."
OK

"The first time a Pawn is moved, it's the player's choice."
OK

"A Pawn that has moved, like the one on f3,..."
OK

MOVE f4
"...may only move one square forward per move."
OK

BOARD 24/4r3/4P3/24 WHITE
"Unlike other pieces, the Pawn cannot capture an opposing piece that lies in 
its path."
OK

"Here, the White Pawn cannot capture the Black Rook."
OK

BOARD 24/5p2/4NQR1/24 WHITE
"A Pawn can only capture a piece on one of the two squares diagonally in 
front of it."
OK

"Here, the Black Pawn can capture either the White Rook or White Knight,"
OK

"but not the White Queen."
OK

BOARD 24/5p2/4NQR1/24 WHITE
SLIDE f5 e4
"Pawn takes Knight."
OK

BOARD 64 WHITE
"Pawns are the least valuable piece.  But don't throw them away 
thoughtlessly.  A single Pawn can sometimes mean the difference between 
winning and losing!"
OK

END CHAPTER

